---
title: Hex shift
tags: tools
heading: "Shift hex"
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% from "macros/delimiter.njk" import delimiter %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
<p class="px-2">
    Lazy shift a hexadecimal string up or down: <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">48 65 6c 6c 6f</code> [Hello] becomes <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">49 66 6d 6d 70</code> [Ifmmp] when shifted 1 to the right (+1) or <code class="d-inline-flex px-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 border border-success border-opacity-10 rounded-2">47 64 6b 6b 6e</code> [Gdkkn] when shifted 1 to the left. 
</p>
<p class="px-2">
    Your hex can use any of the usual delimiters between bytes (spaces, hyphens, colons, commas, semicolons, new lines, \x, 0x or %), or none, and they can be mixed. The delimiter dropdown chooses how the result is written. Negative numbers are allowed.
</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Shift hex", placeholder = "Example: 48 65 6c 6c 6f", layout = "list", listLabel = "Shifted") %}
<div class="input-group w-auto">
    <label class="input-group-text" for="{{ filename }}Value">Shift<span class="visually-hidden"> each byte by</span></label>
    <input type="number" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Value" autocomplete="off" value="1" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
    <button class="btn btn-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Run">Shift</button>
</div>
<div class="input-group w-auto">
    <label class="input-group-text" for="{{ filename }}Delimiter"><span class="visually-hidden">Hex </span>Delimiter</label>
    {{ delimiter(filename) }}
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
